    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `ownerSegment` field is a derived, read-only DTO value, so it follows the existing pattern for computed owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`) \u2014 declared in the OpenAPI schema and computed in the MapStruct mapper. No entity or database changes were needed.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (after `locality`), documenting the four possible values and the derivation rules.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a new mapping and added the computing method:\n\n```java\ndefault String toOwnerSegment(Owner owner) {\n    String tier = toMembershipLevel(owner) >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n    String area = REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(toLocality(owner)) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n    return tier + \"_\" + area;\n}\n```\n\nThis reuses the existing single-source-of-truth helpers:\n- **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `toMembershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n- **AREA**: `METRO` when the derived `locality` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD \u2014 exactly the keys of the `REGION_TIMEZONE` table), else `REGIONAL` (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSegmentForKnownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) pass, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
